+### 3. ISSUE: ACCEPTANCE_GAP / TEST_GAP (blocking) — the row is not load-bearing
+
+**Manifest `acceptance_criteria[0]` requires:** *"the row FAILS on a copy of the file whose `if err is None:`
+guard in `_scope_matches` is removed (the plan's Step 2)"*. **The job `acceptance` repeats it.** Both are unmet.
+
+I reproduced Step 2 myself. Two runs, one conclusion.
+
+**(a) The plan's own recipe, corrected.** The guardless copy is built by replacing
+`        if err is None:\n            spec = ` with `        if True:\n            spec = ` (1 occurrence,
+at `scripts/compound-v-memory.py:1089`). Run verbatim into `/tmp` as the plan writes it, the copy does
+not test anything — `_SCOPE_CHECK_PATH` is derived from `__file__`'s dirname, so with no sibling
+`compound-v-scope-check.py` next to it the copy dies at `:1633` (`RuntimeError: … No such file or
+directory`) before ever reaching the new row, and the plan's `grep 'no private bytecode cache'` prints
+nothing — an absence a careless reader scores as "it failed". **The plan's Step 2 recipe is itself a
+false-positive proof** (secondary finding, below). With the sibling copied alongside, the copy runs to
+completion:
+
+```
+  ok   matcher missing -> unavailable
+  ok   no private bytecode cache -> unavailable, nothing loaded
+
+0 failed
+all self-tests passed
+```
+
+The guardless copy prints **`ok`**, not `FAIL`. Expected by plan and manifest: `FAIL no private bytecode
+cache -> unavailable, nothing loaded`.
+
+**(b) Marker instrumentation — the hole is real and the row is blind to it.** Same two copies (real,
+guardless) in one scratch directory beside a `compound-v-scope-check.py` whose first line appends one
+byte to a `MARKER` file on execution, so the marker counts how many times the sibling is actually
+imported during one `--selftest`:
+
+| Copy | selftest result | `MARKER` bytes = sibling imports |
+|---|---|---|
+| real `scripts/compound-v-memory.py` | `0 failed / all self-tests passed` | **1** (the parity rows' one legitimate load; the fail-closed row loaded nothing) |
+| guardless (`if True:` at `:1089`) | `0 failed / all self-tests passed` | **2** — the sibling is executed a second time with `sys.pycache_prefix` **never redirected**: precisely the forged-`.pyc` execution the guard exists to prevent |
+
+The guard's removal changes real, observable behaviour — and the selftest stays green either way.
+
+**Root cause (why the row cannot fail).** The row asserts only on the *verdict* and the *note*. Removing
+the `:1089` guard does not change either, because `err` was already set by the `except` branch above, and
+the second guard at `:1105-1109` (`fn = … if err is None else None`; `if err is not None: raise
+RuntimeError(err)`) still raises with the identical message. Measured, both copies, same patched
+`tempfile.mkdtemp`:
+
+```
+real      -> unavailable | scope-check matcher unavailable: refusing to import the scope matcher without a private bytecode cache (no space left)
+guardless -> unavailable | scope-check matcher unavailable: refusing to import the scope matcher without a private bytecode cache (no space left)
+```
+
+Byte-identical. The `:1089` guard governs a **side effect** (whether the module is executed), not the
+returned verdict — so a verdict-only assertion is provably incapable of distinguishing guarded from
+guardless. The row's own title claims *"nothing loaded"* and asserts nothing of the kind. The
+observable the requirement needs — *the sibling module must not be executed when the private cache
+cannot be created* — is exactly what the row does not check.
+
+→ **Sample-audit finding 1 remains OPEN.** The retry did not close it.
